  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Tigloylgomisin H and HCC1937 through a series of target interactions. Tigloylgomisin H is implicated in targeting VMRC-LCP, which is a target of Myxotyroside B, and Myxotyroside B further targets HCC1937. Similarly, Tigloylgomisin H also targets LNCaP, which is a target of a compound with a complex structure, and this compound also targets HCC1937. Additionally, Tigloylgomisin H targets NH-6, which is a target of the same compound, and this compound also targets HCC1937. These findings collectively indicate that Tigloylgomisin H may act through a pathway that ultimately leads to the targeting of HCC1937. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Tigloylgomisin H influences downstream targets that ultimately interact with HCC1937, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
